WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Here's what people
are talking about.

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw that today
a White House adviser

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:06.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
compared President Trump
to Houdini...

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.173 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:11.711
...because, "If you keep him in
a cage, he's going to get out."

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.013 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
When asked how he knows that,
he said,

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:18.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
"'Cause we put him in a cage,
and -- and he got out."

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.953 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah, that's right.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:22.722 line:92%
He said, "Trump's like Houdini."

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:25.792
If you think about it, Trump
is a pretty good magician,

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:26.459 size:88% position:44% line:92%
because in the past year

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
he sawed his approval rating
in half

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:30.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
and made everyone
who worked for him disappear.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:34.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that's not bad.
I'll give it up.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.802 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:36.936 line:92%
In the meantime, Trump keeps

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:39.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
demanding money
for his border wall,

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
even though
there are limited funds.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump is like that couple
on "House Hunters"

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:46.780
who wants a five-bedroom mansion
on a $70,000 budget.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:50.817
It's like, "And it has to
have marble countertops.

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:53.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is a must.
I won't even look at it."

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.821 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
Still, the White House
is calling the deal

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:59.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
that reopened the government
a win for Republicans

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:01.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a loss for
Senator Chuck Schumer.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, we actually
got ahold of Schumer,

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.198 line:92%
and here's what he had to say.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:07.400 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
First he said...

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:12.105 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Then he said...

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.742 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Then he said...

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:20.113 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And then he said...

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:26.152 line:92%
And finally his necklace said...

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:28.321 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:31.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just kept going,
falling as he was --

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:33.193 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:36.162
Meanwhile, the White House
announced new restrictions

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:39.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
on washing machines
imported to the U.S.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's partially
to protect consumers,

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
mainly 'cause Trump was eating
too many Tide Pods.

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:47.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he g--
Don't do that. Don't do that.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw that Melania was
supposed to go to Switzerland

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:53.146
with Donald this week,
but is backing out due to

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.215 size:75% position:38% line:92%
"logistical issues."

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.851
It turns out Melania uses
a lot of different excuses

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get out of things
with her husband.

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:02.922
She even has her own excuse
generator to come up with them.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.357 line:92%
I'll show you how it works.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.291 line:92%
For example, when Donald asks,

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Do you want to join me
at a campaign fundraiser?"

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.563 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
She says...

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:11.731 size:78% position:39% line:92%
"Unfortunately I'm...

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:13.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
actually attending
a fundraiser for...

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:14.901 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oprah."

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:17.670 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It works.
-You see how it works?

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:20.773 line:92%
Next up, when Donald asks,

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Do you want to watch
the Super Bowl with me?"

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.411 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
She says...

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.246 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"I totally would, but...

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:29.282
there's a government shutdown...
in my mind."

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.151 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:32.785 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:33.720 line:92%
-And finally, when Donald asks,

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.456
"Do you want to have dinner
with the British ambassador?"

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
she says...

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I can't,
I have an appointment to...

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.095
take our dog to the vet...
right after I buy us a dog."

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:45.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, that's interesting.
You don't have a dog.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:49.602
Hey. Oscar nominees were
announced today, you guys.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:50.370 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The nominees...

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's exciting.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:53.606 line:92%
Nominees for Best Picture

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:57.844
include "Lady Bird," "Get Out,"
and "The Shape of Water."

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.379 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:02.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
While the favorite for
Worst Picture is still this.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:05.585 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Ooh, that's unfortunate.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.254 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hey, this is cool.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
The History Channel show
"Pawn Stars"

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:12.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
is celebrating
its 500th episode.

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:15.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
To celebrate, the network gave
the producers gold watches,

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
which they immediately knew
were fake.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.265 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:22.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
Finally, I saw that
a grocery store in Scotland

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:23.369 line:92%
had to let an employee go

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
for not being helpful enough
to customers.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:28.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's kind of an odd story.
Take a look at this video.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.475 line:92%
-A Pepper robot named Fabio

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
was recently given
his rolling papers

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:33.112 line:92%
from a Scottish grocery store

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:35.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
after he failed
at, well, being human.

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:37.617 size:81% position:41%
He allegedly would not
listen to directions

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:40.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
and had often directed people
to the alcohol aisle

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:43.990 size:84% position:42%
when it didn't know how
to answer a customer.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:44.824 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:47.594
-The good news is, when they
heard he wasn't helping anyone,

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:49.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
he was immediately hired
by Home Depot.

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:51.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
There you go.
We have a great show tonight.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
Give it up for The Roots,
everybody!

